20:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Leak 1: The ad promise does not match the page headline"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"Symptom"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Click-through rate on the ad is acceptable, but the page bounce rate is above 70% and time-on-page is under 10 seconds. Visitors are arriving and immediately leaving."}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-5 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"What it looks like"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":["An ad running on “project management software for remote teams” lands on a page whose headline reads “The Future of Work, Powered by AI.” The visitor clicked because they want to manage a remote team. The headline tells them nothing about whether they are in the right place. Research by Lindgaard et al. published in"," ",["$","em",null,{"children":"Behaviour & Information Technology"}]," (",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01449290500330448","className":"text-accent hover:text-fg underline","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","children":"doi:10.1080/01449290500330448"}],") found that users form a visual impression of a webpage in approximately 50 milliseconds - before they have read a word. The headline is the first word they read. If it does not confirm the promise, the decision to leave is already forming."]}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-5 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"Self-check"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Copy your ad headline. Open your landing page. Does the page headline contain the same noun phrase - the same specific outcome or audience - as the ad? If you have to interpret or infer the connection, so does a cold visitor."}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-5 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Rewrite the hero headline to echo the ad's specific promise. If the ad says “50% off running shoes for wide feet,”            the page should say “Wide-Fit Running Shoes - 50% Off This Week.” Not a paraphrase - the same nouns. The visitor arrived because of a specific promise; the headline either confirms they are in the right place or it does not. Message-match is signal 1 of the 9 conversion signals the Nebula audit measures, because it shapes whether any of the other signals get a chance to work."}]]}]
21:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Leak 2: Proof is generic, anonymous, or absent"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"Symptom"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Visitors scroll past the hero but abandon before the CTA. Heatmap data (if you have it) shows engagement drop-off around the testimonial or social-proof section."}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-5 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"What it looks like"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"“This product changed my business.” - J.T., Business Owner. That quote is indistinguishable from a placeholder. The visitor does not know if J.T. is real, if their business resembles theirs, or what specifically changed. Proof that cannot be verified does not reduce purchase risk - it increases it, because it signals that genuine evidence may not exist."}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-5 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"Self-check"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Look at each testimonial or proof element on your page. Does it include: a full name (or clearly labelled composite), a specific outcome with a number or timeframe, and enough context for a similar visitor to recognise themselves? If not, it is not doing conversion work."}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-5 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Replace generic quotes with specific ones. “We went from 1.2% to 4.1% conversion rate on our SaaS trial page in three weeks” is proof. “Game-changer” is decoration. If you do not have specific testimonials yet, use a before/after case note with enough detail to be falsifiable. One real proof point is more useful to a reader than five vague ones because it can be checked."}]]}]
22:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Leak 3: The CTA does not match where the visitor is in their decision"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"Symptom"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The CTA button exists and is visible, but click rate is low relative to scroll depth. Visitors are reading the page and stopping at the CTA."}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-5 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"What it looks like"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"A page selling a high-consideration engagement leads with “Book Now” as the primary CTA, before any explanation of what the engagement involves, who it is for, or what the outcome is. “Book Now” is the right CTA for a visitor who has already decided - it is the wrong CTA for a visitor who has just arrived. Asking for full commitment before establishing value is the most common pattern in pages we audit."}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-5 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"Self-check"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Read your CTA button text. Does it describe what the visitor gets, or what they have to do? “Book Now” describes what they do. “See How It Works” or “Get Your Diagnosis” describes what they get. For high-consideration purchases, a CTA that offers the next step in the decision process is a useful alternative to test against a final-commitment ask."}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-5 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Match the CTA to the temperature of the traffic. Cold paid traffic landing on a page for the first time is not ready to “Buy.” Offer them the next decision step: a free audit, a demo, a specific deliverable. Reserve “Buy Now” or “Book Now” for pages where visitors have already consumed proof and understand the offer. Also check form friction: if the form asks for more fields than the next step requires, each extra field is a reason to stop."}]]}]
23:["$","div",null,{"className":"my-6 rounded-2xl border border-accent/40 bg-bg-panel p-6","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-accent mb-1","children":"Not sure which leak is active on your page?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-fg-muted text-sm mb-4","children":"Run the free Nebula audit. It checks all 9 conversion signals and tells you which one is breaking the sequence."}],["$","$L19",null,{"href":"/audit?utm_source=learning-centre&utm_medium=organic-content","className":"inline-flex rounded bg-accent px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-bg hover:opacity-85 hover:bg-accent transition-colors","children":"Run the free audit"}]]}]
24:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Leak 4: The mobile experience breaks the message"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"Symptom"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Desktop conversion rate runs higher than mobile, despite mobile accounting for the majority of paid traffic clicks. The gap is not a device-preference issue - it is a layout problem."}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-5 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"What it looks like"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"On desktop, the hero section shows a headline, a subheadline, a proof point, and a CTA button - all above the fold. On mobile at 390px, the headline wraps to four lines, the subheadline disappears, and the CTA button is below the fold before the user has scrolled. The visitor sees a wall of text and a button they have to hunt for. The message sequence - promise, proof, action - is intact on desktop and broken on mobile."}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-5 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"Self-check"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Open your landing page on a real phone (not a browser emulator). Without scrolling: do you see a clear headline, at least one proof signal, and a CTA button? If the button is not visible without scrolling, many visitors will not scroll far enough to find it."}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-5 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Design the above-fold mobile layout as the primary canvas, not a scaled-down version of desktop. The headline should be under 10 words to avoid wrapping to four lines. The CTA must be a full-width tap target visible without scrolling. Social proof can move below fold on mobile - the headline and CTA cannot. Test on a real device, not a browser emulator; emulators do not replicate thumb reach, font rendering, or how the browser chrome eats viewport height."}]]}]
25:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Leak 5: Objections are not handled before the final ask"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"Symptom"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Visitors scroll all the way to the bottom CTA and still do not convert. Scroll depth is high, time-on-page is reasonable, but the final conversion rate is low. The page has their attention - it has not resolved their hesitation."}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-5 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"What it looks like"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"A SaaS trial page shows features, pricing, and a sign-up CTA but does not address: how long setup takes, whether a credit card is required, what happens when the trial ends, or who to contact if something breaks. These are four questions a realistic buyer has before they enter their email. If the page does not answer them, the visitor leaves to find the answers - and often does not come back."}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-5 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"Self-check"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"List the three main reasons a qualified buyer would not convert on your page. Now check whether each reason is addressed - not in your FAQ, but on the page, above or adjacent to the final CTA. If the answers are buried or absent, the objection is a live conversion blocker."}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-5 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Add a three-item objection block directly above your final CTA. Format it as specific answers, not marketing copy. “No credit card required” is an objection answer. “Risk-free trial” is marketing copy - it raises the question of what “risk-free” means and who defined it."}]]}]
26:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Which leak do you fix first?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-5 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The five leaks above are the failure modes a founder experiences; the 9 conversion signals are what the Nebula audit measures - each signal maps to the leak it surfaces. Fix in signal order. Earlier signals act as gates: if signal 1 is broken, fixing signal 6 does nothing."}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"space-y-5","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-5 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-accent","children":"Signal 1 - Message match"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-fg","children":"Test:"}]," ","Does the headline echo the ad promise exactly?"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm text-fg-muted","children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-fg","children":"If no:"}]," ","Fix this first. Nothing else matters until visitors know they are in the right place."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-xs text-fg-subtle","children":["Surfaces: ","Leak 1"]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-5 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-accent","children":"Signal 2 - Trust signals"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-fg","children":"Test:"}]," ","Is there at least one specific, verifiable proof point above the fold?"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm text-fg-muted","children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-fg","children":"If no:"}]," ","Add before optimising the CTA. The CTA can only convert visitors who believe the offer. Unresolved purchase objections are also a trust failure - this signal surfaces both Leak 2 and Leak 5."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-xs text-fg-subtle","children":["Surfaces: ","Leaks 2 and 5"]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-5 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-accent","children":"Signal 3 - Mobile viewport"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-fg","children":"Test:"}]," ","Is the primary CTA visible on a real phone without scrolling?"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm text-fg-muted","children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-fg","children":"If no:"}]," ","Fix before running mobile traffic. Desktop conversion data does not transfer to a broken mobile experience."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-xs text-fg-subtle","children":["Surfaces: ","Leak 4"]}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-5 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-accent","children":"Signal 4 - Load speed"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-fg","children":"Test:"}]," ","Does the page load in under 3 seconds on a mobile connection?"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm text-fg-muted","children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-fg","children":"If no:"}]," ",["Slow load time bleeds conversions before the page is seen. Not covered by the five-leak model above - covered in depth in"," ",["$","$L19",null,{"href":"/learning-centre/landing-page-load-time-slow","className":"text-accent hover:text-fg underline","children":"Landing Page Load Time Slow"}],"."]]}],null]}],["$","li","4",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-5 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-accent","children":"Signal 5 - CTA clarity"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-fg","children":"Test:"}]," ","Does the CTA describe what the visitor gets, not what they have to do?"]}],"$L3a","$L3b"]}],"$L3c","$L3d","$L3e","$L3f"]}]]}]
27:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-6 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Frequently asked questions"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","div","What is the most common reason a landing page does not convert?",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"What is the most common reason a landing page does not convert?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"A broken promise between the ad and the page headline. When the ad says '50% off running shoes' and the page headline says 'Shop Our Collection,' the visitor has no confirmation they are in the right place and leaves. This is what the message-match signal in Nebula's 9-signal audit framework measures."}]]}],["$","div","How do I know if my landing page conversion rate is actually low?",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"How do I know if my landing page conversion rate is actually low?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"WordStream's 2026 Google Ads Benchmarks report - analysing over 13,000 search advertising campaigns from April 2025 to March 2026 - found an all-industries median conversion rate of 8.18%, ranging from 2.64% in Finance and Insurance to 16.22% in Animals and Pets. These are median figures across Google and Microsoft Ads search campaigns, not single-page rates, but they give a realistic floor for your vertical. If you are consistently below your vertical's lower bound with meaningful traffic (500+ sessions), that suggests evaluating structural page friction as a candidate cause."}]]}],["$","div","Should I A/B test my landing page before diagnosing the problem?",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"Should I A/B test my landing page before diagnosing the problem?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"No. A/B testing is a measurement tool, not a diagnostic tool. Testing two versions of a page with a broken promise doubles your spend on the wrong problem. Diagnose the leak first - identify which of the five patterns is active - then test the fix against the control."}]]}],["$","div","What is message match and why does it matter?",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"What is message match and why does it matter?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Message match is the degree to which your landing page headline repeats or reinforces the specific promise in the ad that brought the visitor there. A visitor who clicked 'Free 30-day trial for SaaS teams' expects to see those words, or close equivalents, immediately on the page. When they do not, they assume they clicked the wrong link and leave. High message match reduces the first decision a visitor has to make: am I in the right place?"}]]}],["$","div","How long does it take to fix a non-converting landing page?",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"How long does it take to fix a non-converting landing page?"}],"$L40"]}]]}]]}]
